I, Vitalii Skikun, solved the halting problem, it doesn't exist. Just
check every n + 1 clock cycles whether the previous savestate (a term
from speedrunning) matches the current savestate exactly, byte for byte.
You can discard the previous previous savestate.

n can be a arbitrary precision integer. You add 1 to n every time you
check. Also, my algorithm detects all infinite loops, but some infinite
loops may be whitelisted like the OS kernel.

Now where's my million dollars for proving P=NP...

